def table(rows,keys):
 def fmt(x):return f'{x:,.2f}' if isinstance(x,float) else str(x)
 return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+html.escape(k.replace('_',' '))+'</th>' for k in keys)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(fmt(r[k]))+'</td>' for k in keys)+'</tr>' for r in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
def link(name,label):return '<a href="../../../processed/three_ward_transport_framework_v1/'+name+'">'+label+'</a>'
body=f'''<h1>Three-ward transport-isolation framework</h1><p class="lead">Official 2020 resident counts now supply the nighttime aggregate baseline. The transport data support a concrete inventory and tested flood-grid interface, while a complete, current routable multimodal graph remains to be qualified. No isolation or stranded-person counts have been calculated.</p>
<div class="cards"><div><b>4,746</b><br>census basic units</div><div><b>496,345</b><br>historical residents</div><div><b>154</b><br>core station-line records</div><div><b>{pa['unique_gml_id_geometry_variants']}</b><br>regional PLATEAU access candidates</div></div>
<p>Of the 85 PLATEAU underground-access inventory points, 25 fall within the three-ward core and 60 outside it; the package mesh footprints extend past ward boundaries. These outside candidates remain context, not core entrance counts or a verified complete entrance inventory.</p><p>N02 station-line records include JR 35, Tokyo Metro 73, Toei 35 and other operators 11. Their 85 source station-group candidates are matching aids, not 85 verified interchange complexes. Keep other operators and through-running where relevant before making a multimodal isolation claim.</p>
<img src="transport_inventory_overview.png" alt="Regional railway inventory and partial historical walking network coverage">
<h2>What was acquired and checked</h2>'''
body+=table(sources,['layer','status','coverage','epoch','supports','missing'])
body+='''<h2>The analysis chain</h2><div class="chain">Fixed census block totals → uncertain local access support → pedestrian / road graph → station entrance and platform graph → service-specific metro / JR graph → future connectivity and accessibility outcomes</div>
<p>Existing inundation modifies the relevant ground-road and station-approach links at the same actual time. Explicit rail service scenarios modify different edges. Population, hazard and service remain separate inputs. A census block, a hydraulic connected component and a passenger-network island are different objects.</p>
<h2>1. Network construction rules</h2><p>Walking and vehicle access use separate permissions and directions. Grade-separated crossings connect only through real ramps, crossings, stairs or lifts. A relative floor or layer number is not metres of elevation. Preserve stable source IDs, survey epochs and unknown fields. The GSI sample contains geometry and width/state attributes but no verified complete vehicle restriction model.</p>
<p>N02 legal-route names are not train operating systems: for example, the inventory has only one core station record under the legal Yamanote-line label, while the operating Yamanote loop uses other legal rail corridors as well. Do not build a JR service network by sorting names or coordinates alone.</p><p>A station entrance, ticket gate, concourse, platform, boarding link and running-service link have separate roles. N02 supplies station geometry as a line; neither its midpoint nor its same-name/300 m grouping proves a valid entrance or transfer. Do not join all rail intersections, nearby stations or roads to a station centroid.</p>
<h2>2. Necessary external connections</h2><p>The 5 km road halo and 20 km rail inventory are initial acquisition extents, not validated model boundaries. National rail data remain retained. Keep full usable approaches, river crossings, neighboring interchanges and relevant through-running services to predeclared external destinations. Later compare an expanded 10 km road extent and enlarge further if core accessibility or detours change. An outer clipped node is not automatically a legitimate or safe destination.</p>
<p>Links outside the hydraulic footprint have unknown flood conditions. Compare explicit availability/impairment assumptions rather than silently treating them as dry. Extent sensitivity and unknown-boundary sensitivity must be checked before claiming an isolated district.</p>
<h2>3. Coupling existing inundation</h2><p>The existing qualified train-06 output directly exposes zs, h, u, v and subgrid volume at 49 actual-clock states. Coordinates match the canonical 10 m EPSG:6677 grid. GDAL reports identity raster georeferencing for this NetCDF, so blindly overlaying its default transform would be wrong: the adapter must use verified x/y arrays and the saved affine.</p>
<p>For a verified surface travel level, use h_road(t) = max(0, eta(t) − z_travel_surface), retaining wet-state, shallow censoring, quality and vertical-datum checks. The existing open-ground mean-depth label is a screening quantity; it is not pointwise entrance, kerb, bridge-deck or tunnel water depth. Quarantined, outside-domain and unproved-elevation locations remain unknown.</p>
<p>The sparse candidate edge-cell interface has been generated and its intersected lengths conserve the length inside the model rectangle. This establishes geometry and indexing only, not passability. The maps are roughly five minutes apart; exact short-duration failure and recovery cannot be recovered from them. Cellwise peak depths can define a stress envelope but must not be combined into a simultaneous closure map or isolation duration.</p>
<h2>4. Station access versus railway operation</h2><p>Flooded ground approaches can impair access. Closing one entrance disables that access link; other entrances and through trains may remain available. Station non-stop operation, a platform closure, a running-section suspension and a full-line suspension are separate declared states. Local surface water alone does not predict operator shutdown decisions, tunnel flooding or pumps/barriers. No safety depth, speed or shutdown threshold is selected in this audit.</p>
<h2>5. Fixed population and retained building uncertainty</h2><p>The official 2020 count is fixed for each block. Keep the prior 125/250 m building scenarios and conditional envelopes as a separate sidecar. Do not add building counts to census totals, allocate a whole block at its centroid or silently rescale the old mesh-constrained interval endpoints. If a future network component divides a block, keep location unresolved with conservative support subject to the fixed block total until a new constrained within-block allocation is qualified.</p>
<p>Night resident population is a residential stock, not observed occupancy at the storm time, a departure-time assumption or an OD trip matrix. Use a matched operating-calendar baseline: a normal last-train closure must not be misclassified as a rain-induced shutdown. The 2020 population and later network snapshot describe a conditional exposure scenario, not a coeval observed event.</p>
<h2>Matched future comparisons</h2>'''+table(csvrows(OUT/'scenario_matrix.csv'),['scenario_id','road_state','metro_service_state','jr_service_state','purpose'])
body+='''<p>These are comparison templates; no particular station or line has been selected for closure. Strict no-path, degraded-but-connected accessibility and service interruption must be reported separately. Road/metro/JR contrast results do not establish queues, actual congestion, return-home failure or stranded people without further demand and capacity evidence.</p>
<h2>Priority gaps and the next bounded task</h2>'''+table(gaps,['priority','gap','next_action','release_check'])
body+='''<p><b>Recommended next task:</b> construct and qualify the dry pedestrian / road topology over the core and external approaches, batch-check grade and seams, and link the station inventory to verified service/access candidates. Report coverage, unmapped origins and topology gaps first. Only then apply the matched hazard/service states. No extra hydraulic scenarios or ML training are needed for that step.</p>
<h2>Deliverables and checks</h2><ul>'''
for name,label in [('framework_contract.json','Framework and interpretation contract'),('network_schema.json','Node, edge, state and population-link schemas'),('source_audit.csv','Source audit: scope, epoch, fields and gaps'),('data_gaps.csv','Prioritized data and validation gaps'),('scenario_matrix.csv','Matched comparison templates'),('night_population_baseline.csv','Fixed nighttime census block totals'),('core_rail_corridor_inventory.csv','Core and external railway corridor inventory'),('walking_candidate_nodes.csv','Historical walking candidate nodes'),('walking_candidate_edges.csv','Historical walking candidate edges'),('walking_edge_hazard_cells.csv','Verified geometric edge-to-flood-grid interface'),('historical_station_access_candidates.csv','Historical station-associated access candidates'),('plateau_underground_access_candidates_6677.geojson','PLATEAU underground-access candidates'),('provisional_road_tile_requests.csv','Provisional regional road acquisition requests')]:body+='<li>'+link(name,label)+'</li>'
body+='''<li><a href="hazard_interface_audit.json">Actual-clock and coordinate audit</a>; <a href="validation.json">interface checks</a>; <a href="plateau_access_audit.json">PLATEAU access audit</a>; <a href="delivery_manifest.json">version bindings</a></li></ul>
<h2>Official sources and access status</h2><p><a href="https://nlftp.mlit.go.jp/ksj/gml/datalist/KsjTmplt-N02-2025.html">MLIT N02</a>; <a href="https://github.com/gsi-cyberjapan/experimental_rdcl">GSI road centre lines</a>; <a href="https://www.geospatial.jp/ckan/dataset/0401">MLIT walking-network catalog and field specification</a>; <a href="https://ckan.odpt.org/dataset/r_station-tokyometro">Tokyo Metro station catalog</a>; <a href="https://ckan.odpt.org/dataset/r_route-toei">Toei route catalog</a>; <a href="https://ckan.odpt.org/dataset/jreast__r_route">JR East route catalog</a>.</p>
<p>N02 is CC BY 4.0; walking data follow the linked government terms; GSI attribution and terms remain applicable. Metro and JR catalogs carry their own licenses; JR East station/route resources are currently explicitly Challenge 2026 limited. Catalog verification is not permission or proof of complete payload availability. No account was registered or restricted transit payload fetched. Direct scripted station-page requests returned 403 and were retained as blocked receipts; current provider pages were inspected through the read-only browser. Old Metro API exit documentation is not treated as proof of a current entrance API.</p>
<p>OSM is an optional permission/entrance supplement with <a href="https://download.geofabrik.de/asia/japan/kanto.html">dated Kanto extracts</a> and ODbL requirements. No large OSM archive was downloaded. OSM relative-layer and entrance tags require independent completeness and station matching checks.</p>
<p>No original census allocation, model result, train/validation partition or sealed response was modified. The live AnaSOP is unchanged; this scoped framework records the accepted transport direction without treating the old surrogate objective as current.</p>'''
